==Latin==

===Alternative forms===
* [[alium]]

===Etymology===
From {{der|la|ine-pro|*ālu||esculent root}}, uncertainly reconstructed. Related only to {{cog|sa|आलु||esculent root}}<ref>Mallory, Encyclopedia of Indo-European Culture</ref>, whence {{cog|hi|आलु||potato, yam}}, and the culinary borrowing, {{cog|en|aloo||potato}}.

Alternatively, Kroonen suggests that it may be a borrowing from the root of {{bor|la|grc|ἄγλις}}, specifically via a byform ''*adlī-*''. See the Ancient Greek entry for more.<ref>{{cite-journal|title=An Akkadian loanword in Pre-Greek: on the etymology of Greek ἄγλις and γέλγις 'garlic'|author=Kroonen, Guus|authorlink=Guus Kroonen|journal=The Journal of Indo-European Studies|url=http://www.academia.edu/2604857/An_Akkadian_loanword_in_Pre-Greek_on_the_etymology_of_Greek_%E1%BC%84%CE%B3%CE%BB%CE%B9%CF%82_and_%CE%B3%CE%AD%CE%BB%CE%B3%CE%B9%CF%82_garlic|volume=40|year=2012|pages=289-299}}</ref>

